&lt;div id=&#34;p1&#34; class=&#34;ltx_para&#34;&gt;
&lt;p class=&#34;ltx_p&#34;&gt;The Greek Letters are used widely in LaTeX mathematical equation typesetting. Due to a long history of cultural transmission and regional variation, some letters have developed distinct script forms. Overleaf provides an excellent guide &lt;cite class=&#34;ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite&#34;&gt;[&lt;a href=&#34;#bib.bib1&#34; title=&#34;List of greek letters and math symbols&#34; class=&#34;ltx_ref&#34;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;]&lt;/cite&gt; on Greek Letters that helped me considerably. However, after discussing with Claude AI, I found it incomplete. This article records a complete list for understanding and daily practical writing in LaTeX. The basic information is from the Wikipedia article on the Greek alphabet &lt;cite class=&#34;ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite&#34;&gt;[&lt;a href=&#34;#bib.bib3&#34; title=&#34;Greek alphabet&#34; class=&#34;ltx_ref&#34;&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;]&lt;/cite&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
